\details{
Wraps the ESPN core-v2 single-team power-index endpoint
\code{sports.core.api.espn.com/v2/sports/football/leagues/college-football/seasons/{year}/powerindex/{team_id}}.
Where \code{\link[=espn_cfb_powerindex]{espn_cfb_powerindex()}} returns the league-wide index, this wrapper
drills into one team and returns one row per metric in long format: every
predictive metric (FPI, projected wins, strength of record, ...) and every
efficiency component (offensive, defensive, special-teams efficiency, ...).
The long shape is deliberate -- ESPN adds and retires metrics across
seasons, and a long frame absorbs that drift. Pivot wider with
\code{\link[tidyr:pivot_wider]{tidyr::pivot_wider()}} keyed on \code{stat_name} for a wide table.

When \code{team_detail = TRUE} (the default) the ESPN team catalog
(\code{\link[=espn_cfb_teams]{espn_cfb_teams()}}) is fetched once and friendly team fields are joined
in next to the \code{team_id} column -- \code{team_name}, \code{team_abbreviation},
\code{team_location}, \code{team_display_name}, \code{team_short_display_name},
\code{team_nickname}, \code{team_color}, \code{team_alternate_color},
\code{team_logo_href}, and \code{team_logo_dark_href}, inserted immediately after
\code{team_id}.
A catalog failure degrades to \code{NA} rather than erroring the wrapper. Set
\code{team_detail = FALSE} to skip the catalog fetch and the join.
